$DIR/main.p:11:4: union type must be the type of a type definition: type U union { ... }
    A union type can only be the type of a type definition, type U union { ...
    }. It cannot be written inline in a variable or field, or be an alias,
    because its variants are reached through its name (U.V).
    (see "Unions" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2401" for a longer explanation)

